  "justiceSays": [
    {
      "day": 6,
      "line": "Marcus has been asking about the strange leaves all week — \"but what IS it?\" Tonight, an answer. Fireside lesson: Hans passes around tall smooth stalks turning reddish-purple, with dark purple berry clusters in late summer. Someone asks a dumb question. Nobody minds. That's how you learn."
    },
    {
      "day": 6,
      "line": "★ IDENTIFIED: Pokeweed. Smooth stalks, purple-red stems, dark berry clusters. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."
    },
    {
      "day": 10,
      "line": "Word reaches you, days late: Sofia stands accused over what happened to Yara. There's going to be a moot. People are choosing sides."
    },
    {
      "day": 11,
      "line": "Hans has been talking at the fires. Enough voices — tonight they call a moot. Sofia answers for what happened to Yara."
    },
    {
      "day": 11,
      "line": "Hans calls the moot. The fire gets built up — word travels fast, and almost everyone comes."
    },
    {
      "day": 11,
      "line": "The moot turns to you. Your vote matters here — and everyone will remember it."
    },
    {
      "day": 12,
      "line": "Word reaches you, days late: Lena stands accused over what happened to Aroha. There's going to be a moot. People are choosing sides."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "The moot doesn't wait forever. Two days of silence from the fire's edge — the count is taken without you."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "The fire is built high. Nobody speaks while the count is taken — you can hear the wind past the edge of the light."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "Hans counts on their fingers, twice, like they don't trust the first number. Then, to the fire: \"0 for guilty. 6 against.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "A long exhale moves around the fire like weather. \"Not guilty — this time.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "line": "Aroha has been talking at the fires. Enough voices — tonight they call a moot. Lena answers for what happened to Aroha."
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "line": "Aroha calls the moot. The fire gets built up — word travels fast, and almost everyone comes."
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "line": "The moot turns to you. Your vote matters here — and everyone will remember it."
    },
    {
      "day": 16,
      "line": "The moot doesn't wait forever. Two days of silence from the fire's edge — the count is taken without you."
    },
    {
      "day": 16,
      "line": "The fire is built high. Nobody speaks while the count is taken — you can hear the wind past the edge of the light."
    },
    {
      "day": 16,
      "line": "Hans counts on their fingers, twice, like they don't trust the first number. Then, to the fire: \"1 for guilty. 6 against.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 16,
      "line": "A long exhale moves around the fire like weather. \"Not guilty — this time.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 49,
      "line": "Emberhold watches to see if Haven holds without its dead. The bond is young — they're still deciding what Haven is, and grief delays the verdict. They'll test the link — count on it, unless Haven answers first: send grain (1,500 kcal), send a speaker (2 days), or let the silence answer. (Trust -8.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 49,
      "line": "🔍 Erich has been turning over a tree heavy with smooth-skinned fruit blushing red and gold for days — today it clicked. \"I know this one now. Look — see the leaves?\""
    },
    {
      "day": 50,
      "line": "Aroha showed Emma the tree heavy with smooth-skinned fruit blushing red and gold — \"remember it.\" Word travels before the lesson cools."
    },
    {
      "day": 84,
      "line": "★ IDENTIFIED: Wild Ramps. Broad smooth leaves, onion smell. Spring only. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."
    }
